      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T10:57:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW I do not know details about vLAPIC but just start thinking based on description and comments: if the sipi_vector is overwritten by pKVM can a malicious host overwrite it again or we are protected somehow from that? What I mean is does those scenario could happen:\n1) we\u0027ve reach this line and the sipi_vector is overwritten by pKVM with expected value but just after that can malicious host which emulates LAPIC overwrite it again before we run this vCPU for the first time?\n2) Can the malicious host at arbitrary time overwrite cs segment (sipi_vector) and trigger vCPU reset (via INIT/SIPI) and cause the vCPU executing malicious code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 801,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 801,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "58edd2c95993629f13c1e681f20d4db6b5701387",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b243213_825f63ab",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 801,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T11:30:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe we should sanitize pv VCPU interface and not allow setting arbitrary segment, because now it seems to be too permissive and allow to set arbitrary segment unconditionally:\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/common/+/android16-6.12-desktop:arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c;l\u003d639 and now pkvm high can set any segment through:\narch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm_high.c: `pkvm_set_segment` (which triggers pkvm version of pkvm_set_segment)\n\nThis pv VCPU interface allows to change the segment only for vcpu that didn\u0027t run yet (checks !kvm_vcpu_has_run(vcpu)) so 2) scenario from my prev comment seems not possible thanks to this check but 1) remains a possibility? WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "959da7fa_8e6ee16b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 801,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 801,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "58edd2c95993629f13c1e681f20d4db6b5701387",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c84243f_00e42495",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 801,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T14:14:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This pv VCPU interface allows to change the segment only for vcpu that didn\u0027t run yet (checks !kvm_vcpu_has_run(vcpu)) so 2) scenario from my prev comment seems not possible thanks to this check\n\nExactly.\n\n\u003e but 1) remains a possibility?\n\nDo you mean that since there is a time window when pKVM has already done pkvm_vcpu_ap_entry_init() but kvm_vcpu_has_run(vcpu) is still false, during this time window the host may make another PV call and successfully modify a segment or anything else that pKVM has set up in pkvm_vcpu_ap_entry_init()?\n\nIt doesn\u0027t seem so. The host may only do that on another CPU, and on that other CPU it will not succeed to do that, since this vCPU is not loaded on that other CPU, so pKVM will not allow it (see the checks in load_pkvm_vcpu()).",
      "parentUuid": "5b243213_825f63ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 801,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 801,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "58edd2c95993629f13c1e681f20d4db6b5701387",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "108eb5a4_a534dc6a",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
