      },
      "lineNbr": 803,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-23T21:10:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking loudly: if malicious host kicks vcpu not as a consequence of PKVM_GHC_START_CPU triggered by pVM but because it is malicious: do I understand correctly that we could start running this function in pKVM hyp with not initialized sipi_vector?\n\nIn `pkvm_vm_init` we `memset(pkvm_vm, 0, pa_size);` so sipi_vector will be set to 0 but not sure if it is safe? WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 798,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 803,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "58edd2c95993629f13c1e681f20d4db6b5701387",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
