    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c8a497b_b80ffb92",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 10052,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-23T22:45:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we skip this part, we still don\u0027t skip the receiver part in kvm_apic_accept_events() which handles KVM_APIC_INIT and KVM_APIC_SIPI and, in particular, does make hypercalls to pKVM to set up the segments in VMCS according to this sipi_vector (which are later overwritten by pKVM anyway, though). So, those host\u0027s actions are useless either way, but if we skip this part, they are useless _and_ inconsistent.\n\nAlthough, thinking more about this... That inconsistency wouldn\u0027t be a big deal, whereas the fact that we _expose_ this start_ip value to the host in the first place seems like a problem. We probably shouldn\u0027t even expose it (e.g. should zero it in pKVM before forwarding the hypercall to the host), since a pVM, in the general case, may not want the host to know it.",
      "parentUuid": "5251871b_8550cf71",
